From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=EC=8B=AC=EC=83=81=EC=9B=90?= <dev.chamomile@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:34:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: GICv3 without an ITS uses a GICv2m MSI frame

Why: Hypervisor.framework's GICv3 has no ITS, which upstream needs for
PCI MSI-X.

What: the GICv3 layout follows Hypervisor.framework's, the ITS is
optional, and without it MSIs go to the GIC's MSI frame, described in the
FDT as `arm,gic-v2m-frame`. GIC state save/restore includes the frame's
SPIs. With an ITS nothing changes. On Linux, where KVM has no MSI frame,
a GICv3 whose ITS cannot be created fails as upstream's does (and
create_gic falls back to GICv2 as upstream's does).

Test: `--enable-pci` with virtio-pci block and net devices on macOS, and a
snapshot restore with PCI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
